# Line-ending policy: store and check out source as LF on every platform.
#
# Without this, the Windows CI runner's `core.autocrlf` converts LF->CRLF on
# checkout, and `cargo fmt --all --check` (rustfmt.toml: newline_style = "Unix")
# then rejects every file with "Incorrect newline style", failing the whole
# `test (windows-latest)` job before clippy/tests ever run. Pinning eol=lf keeps
# the format gate green across the OS matrix.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt-and-suspenders for the format gate and for shell scripts (must be LF).
*.rs   text eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf

# Never normalize binaries (none committed today; future-proofing the policy).
*.png  binary
*.onnx binary
*.gz   binary
*.zip  binary
